Date: Thu, 13 Jan 1994 00:10:20 -0800 (PST)
From: szabo@netcom.com (Nick Szabo)
Subject: Info Bottleneck Rerouting Markets

At the last moment I got word of Allan Schiffman's presentation
on Internet commerce at the local Silly Valley ACM meeting.  
Luckily I made it, and was able to talk to him afterwards.  Schiffman 
is the head of Enterprise Integration Technologies, a big player in the 
local BARNet/CommerceNet efforts, etc.  We covered many 
interesting topics, including the outcome of the BBS porn/K-12 net 
collision, X.12/EDI vs. the IP/MIME-based commercial standards he's 
pushing, trusted entities that issue letters of credit for big trades, 
web of trust vs. trusted public key servers, etc.  Schiffmann rejects
PGP on the grounds that the web of trust model is not viable for business.

A major theme was how Internet commerce might give us a much better
capability to route around information-provider bottlenecks.  Examples 
include the Amercian Airlines/Sabre control of airline ticket
allocation,  "GM-Net" vs. "Ford-Net" (two incompapable CAD transfer
formats that have served to lock in major automaker's suppliers),
a local Silly Valley company that controls information available to
real esate agents, etc.  On this list we've discussed excess taxation,
the credit rating system, etc.   When an information monopoly abuses
its position by discriminating against certain customers (porn
customers, racism that shuts out wealthy ethnics, whatever),
this opens up a market opportunity to route around the failure
by setting up a new information distribution system.

Here are some basic questions that might be quite lucrative
to explore:

* What are currently the biggest market failures (caused either
by government or inefficient  info-monopoly), in terms 
of market volume?

* Which of these bottlenecks are the easiest to route around?  Ie,
which can be tackled by very small "Mom&Pop" entities?  Which
can be tackled with today's off-the-shelf tools?

* Which of these failures have the biggest $volume/rerouting cost
ratio?

* What software tools are both crucial for "info-biz rerouting" and
common across a large market-volume?

